t keys) (count (distinct (map #(bytes-key (cbor/encode %)) keys)))))\n   560\t               (bad! :duplicate-key [id])))))\n   561\t       (letfn [(expand-slot\n   562\t                 [d x]\n   563\t                 (cond (ref? d) (expand x) (refs? d) (mapv expand x)\n   564\t                       (and (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d) (= :row (first x))) [:row (expand (second x))]\n   565\t                       :else x))\n   566\t               (expand\n   567\t                 [id]\n   568\t                 (let [[_ kind & slots] (get index id)]\n   569\t                   (node kind (mapv expand-slot (descriptors kind slots) slots))))]\n   570\t         (let [task (expand root)\n   571\t               _ (check-abstract! task)\n   572\t               canonical (if (= :task (:kind task)) (emit task budget)\n   573\t                             (let [[id _] (emit-node task {} {})] {:yin.k/root id}))]\n   574\t           (when (and (not= false (:check-numbering budget)) (not= root (:yin.k/root canonical)))\n   575\t             (bad! :noncanonical-cursor-cells [root]))\n   576\t           (when (= :task (:kind task))\n   577\t             (when-let [d (validate-frames task)]\n   578\t               (throw (ex-info \"Frame validation failed\" (update d :yin.k/path #(into [root] %))))))\n   579\t           task))))))\n   580\t\n   581\t\n   582\t(defn decode\n   583\t  \"Validate and expand a row pack, including canonical cursor-cell numbering.\n   584\t   For task roots, run X1 and frame validation after numbering.\"\n   585\t  ([wire] (decode* wire default-budget))\n   586\t  ([wire budget] (decode* wire (dissoc budget :check-numbering))))\n   587\t\n   588\t\n   589\t(defn canonical-under\n   590\t  \"Test-only §5.5 re-emission under an explicit stream correspondence.\n   270\tonly the row kinds its table entry names; a `[:row B]` whose target is\n   271\tof another kind refuses (§8). Keyed rows (`:bindings`, `:map`, `:store`,\n   272\t`:parked-table`, `:cursor-cells`, the installs and module-stores slots) must\n   273\thave unique keys, and `:set` rows unique elements, under canonical bytes\n   274\t**and** under portable decoded equality, since Jing's own map and set\n   275\trules do not apply to a key or element list spelled as a vector.\n   276\t\n   277\t### 5.1 Values (content rows)\n   278\t\n   279\t| Kind | Slots | Decodes to |\n   280\t|---|---|---|\n   281\t| `:vec` | `V …` in order | vector |\n   282\t| `:list` | `V …` in order | list |\n   283\t| `:set` | `V …` sorted (§5 preamble) | set |\n   284\t| `:map` | `k₁ V₁ k₂ V₂ …`, each `kᵢ` a `V`, sorted by key | map |\n   285\t| `:bindings` | `S₁ V₁ S₂ V₂ …` sorted by symbol | `{S V}` |\n   286\t| `:env` | `bindings-cref  store-of` | E: the named environment plus, when `store-of` is an `M`, `engine/store-of-key` (amendment §2) |\n   287\t| `:closure` | `segment-A  entry-pc-N  params  bindings-cref  store-of` | semantic closure (amendment §6 semantic arm); `params` is a plain vector of symbols checked against the addressed lambda |\n   288\t| `:prim` | `name-S` | the named primitive after the profile check (UCF §7.5.2); the profile lives in requires |\n   289\t| `:stream` | `identity  descriptor` | a stream marker; both plain, authenticated at lift and re-sealed at lower |\n   290\t| `:reified` | `act-cref` | a captured continuation: the decoded act state of frozen §4.2, no pending |\n   291\t| `:parked-ref` | `parked-id-P` | the keyed `act` state (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §1.2) reached through `P`: resolves in the task's parked table; never duplicates the state |\n   292\t\n   293\t`:reified` and `:parked-ref` keep the two outer discriminants amendment\n   294\t§6 requires and lower differently: a reified value becomes a\n   295\treceiver-owned native continuation from its act; a parked reference\n   296\treconstructs the engine's parked value for `P`. A reified value's act is\n   297\tvalidated in context `:captured` (continuation §3.2 P3): its `pc−1` is a\n   298\t`:current-continuation` and it has no pending.\n   299\t\n   300\t### 5.2 Frame rows: states, windows, waits, frames (content rows)\n   301\t\n   302\t(Replaced 2026-10-11 by `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md`\n   303\t§2.3, under frozen `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §4.2.)\n   304\t\n   305\t| Kind | Slots | Notes |\n   306\t|---|---|---|\n   307\t| `:act` | `segment-A  pc-N  env-cref  window-cref  k-cref  rd-N` | the delivery record is `{:deliver :rd :rd rd-N}` by kind |\n   308\t| `:tail` | `segment-A  site-N  k-cref` | delivery `{:deliver :return}` by kind; **no** env, window or pc slot |\n   309\t| `:window` | `r₁ V₁  r₂ V₂  …` sorted by `rᵢ` ascending, unique | `rᵢ` is `N`; **a nil-valued register is present as `rᵢ [:lit nil]`**; the empty window is `[:window]` |\n   310\t| `:k` | `kframe-cref …` outermost first | `[:k]` is the empty continuation |\n   311\t| `:kframe` | `segment-A  pc-N  env-cref  window-cref  rd-N` | one `:return` frame |\n   312\t| `:wait` | `state-cref  pending-cref` | `state-cref` is an `:act` or a `:tail` row |\n   313\t| `:reified` | `act-cref` | a captured continuation value; its act's `pc−1` is a `:current-continuation` |\n   314\t| `:parked-ref` | `parked-id-P` | unchanged |\n   315\t| `:env` | `bindings-cref  store-of` | unchanged (§5.1) |\n   316\t| `:bindings` | `S₁ V₁  S₂ V₂ …` sorted by symbol | unchanged |\n   317\t\n   318\t`:window`, `:bindings`, `:store` and every other tabled keyed row are\n   319\tstructural rows, never a `V`; §4's \"a reference-free collection must be\n   320\t`[:lit d]`\" rule is about guest collections. `rd` on `:act` is redundant\n   321\twith the instruction at `pc−1` and is checked (continuation §3.2 rule\n   322\tA2), as `pc` is redundant with the pending and checked. The frame rows\n   323\tare in bijection with the keyed canonical frame of continuation §1.2\n   324\t(`rows->frame`, `frame->rows`, continuation §2.7).\n   325\t\n   326\t### 5.3 Pending (content rows)\n   327\t\n   328\tOne kind, `:pending`, whose first slot is the reason and whose remaining\n   329\tslots are fixed per reason. The reasons are UCF §7.4.3's closed union as\n   330\tthe amendment r5 required-keys list fixes them; `:park` and\n   331\t`:call-effect` are not reasons and refuse as `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n   332\t\n   333\t| reason | slots after the reason |\n   334\t|---|---|\n   335\t| `:next` | `cursor-cell-C` |\n   336\t| `:put` | `stream-cref  value-V  op-id-D` |\n   337\t| `:ffi` | `cursor-cell-C  call-id-D  op` (op may be nil) |\n   338\t| `:ffi-request` | `call-id-D  envelope-V  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  response-cursor-cell-C  op-id-D` |\n   339\t| `:link-request` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C  envelope-D  op-id-D` |\n   340\t| `:link-response` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C` |\n   341\t| `:install` | `name-S` |\n   342\t\n   343\tThe retained FFI request's `envelope-V` is the complete envelope map,\n   344\trecursively encoded under §4's ordinary rules: `[:lit m]` when it\n   345\treaches no reference (the common case, arguments such as `[1 2]`), a\n   346\t`:map` row otherwise. Lower decodes it and retries it verbatim; it\n   347\tnever recomputes the arguments. Correlation must agree, not merely be present:\n   348\ta cursor cell's `:cursor-cell-body` stream is the pending's response stream; an\n   349\tenvelope's link id or call id equals the pending's; a `:link-request`\n   350\tenvelope names the pending's module. `op-id` is `{:yin.k/occurrence P :yin.k/seq n}` as plain data or nil,\n   351\tpresent exactly when the write was first attempted through a fenced\n   352\twriter, carried verbatim, never minted or renumbered by lift or lower,\n   353\tand subject to every rule of §7.4.3 r5 (below the root's\n   354\t`:yin.k/next-op-seq`, unique across the task and its children, absent\n   355\twhen the body has no origin). `request-envelope` and `envelope` are the\n   356\tretained requests, retried verbatim. `call-id` and `link-id` are plain.\n   357\tAn `:install` pending is never sufficient alone: the root's installs\n   358\tslot must hold the entry for `name`, else lift refuses\n   359\t`:yin.k/non-portable` kind `:incomplete-install` and a body carrying it\n   360\tis `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n   361\t\n   362\t### 5.4 Task context (content rows)\n   363\t\n   364\t| Kind | Slots |\n   365\t|---|---|\n   366\t| `:store` | `k₁ V₁ k₂ V₂ …` sorted by key; the isolated slice of UCF §7.6.2 |\n   367\t| `:module-store` | `manifest-M  store-cref` |\n   368\t| `:parked-table` | `P₁ state-cref₁ P₂ state-cref₂ …` sorted by P (each state an `:act` or a `:tail`) |\n   369\t| `:install` | `name-S  phase  parent-D  response-D  child-cref` |\n   370\t| `:cursor-cells` | the census, §3 |\n   371\t| `:cursor-cell-body` | `stream-cref  position` (position in the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` portable cursor domain) |\n   372\t\n   373\tValidation of a parked state reads decoded task context, never an\n   374\tengine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the task's live\n   375\t`:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n   376\t`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\n   377\tsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n   378\t`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\n   379\t\n   380\tResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\n   381\tthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\n   382\tM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\n   383\tsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\n   384\treachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n   385\t§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\n   386\tcontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\n   387\tchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\n   388\tmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\n   389\tthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\n   390\tid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\n   391\tis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\n   392\tcontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\n   393\tamendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n   394\t\n   395\t### 5.5 The root\n   396\t\n   397\t```clojure\n   398\t[T :task\n   399\t   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\n   400\t   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\n   401\t   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\n   402\t   role             ; :root | :child\n   403\t   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\n   404\t   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\n   405\t   store-cref\n   406\t   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\n   407\t   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\n   408\t   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\n   409\t   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\n   410\t   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \"v4\" vectors verified to hash to their key\n   411\t   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\n   412\t   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\n   413\t   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\n   414\t   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\n   415\t   custody]         ; plain, see below\n   416\t```\n   417\t\n   418\t(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\n   419\t`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\"v4\"` canonical vectors,\n   420\t`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\n   421\tthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\n   422\t\n   423\tKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\n   424\tparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\n   425\tnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\n   426\tneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\n   427\tnever collapsed to one; a task with an empty ready queue may hold several\n   428\tordered waits.\n   429\t\n   430\t`custody` is the custody arm carried as plain data, under the rules of\n   431\t§7.2.1 and amendment §3, by role, kind and policy:\n   432\t\n   433\t| role | kind | policy | `custody` |\n   434\t|---|---|---|---|\n   435\t| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n   436\t| root | blocked / parked | fork | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork}` |\n   437\t| root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n   438\t| root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n   439\t| child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n   440\t\n   441\tThe explicit fork policy spelling projects onto the amendment's\n   442\tempty-header fork representation: a fork root proposes nothing and is\n   443\tnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n   444\t`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. Admission semantics are the governing ones\n   445\tunchanged; only the spelling is new. No body carries an epoch.\n   446\t\n   447\tThe root is a content row and **its id is the transported state's\n   448\taddress**, the `B` of UCF §7.3.4 for this carrier. Occurrence and origin\n   449\tare inside it, as the governing rule keeps them (§10.1). The code map is\n   450\tplain data in the root rather than a row kind: each instruction vector\n   451\tkeeps its own address `A` computed exactly as UCF §7.3.2 computes it, and\n   452\tthe carrier verifies, never recomputes, that address.\n   453\t\n   454\t## 6. Canonical cursor-cell numbering\n   455\t\n   456\tCursor-cell ids must be a function of the state, or two lifts of one state give\n   457\ttwo root ids. Local rules are not enough: a cursor cell's number must depend on\n   458\teverything that distinguishes it, including references to it from\n   459\telsewhere in the task (the review's counterexample: `'a` bound to a set\n   460\tholding cursor cells X and Y with equal bodies, `'b` bound to X; any rule that\n   461\tlooks only at the set and the bodies cannot tell X from Y, but `'b`\n   462\tcan). The numbering is therefore defined over the **whole alias\n   463\ttopology** of the task, and the definition is the reference against\n   464\twhich any algorithm is checked.\n   465\t\n   466\t**What is defined, and what is not claimed.** The canonical numbering\n   467\tis defined as **the output of the procedure below**, which is a function\n   468\tof the state alone: every step depends only on structure, never on a\n   469\tcursor cell's number or on any hash that includes one, so renaming the cursor cells of\n   470\tthe input does not change the output. It is *not* claimed to be the\n   471\tminimum of the root bytes over all `n!` bijections; that is a different\n   472\tdefinition, and a refinement-and-search procedure is not shown to reach\n   473\tit (signature order does not order Merkle bytes). Nor is it claimed that\n   474\tcursor cells left together by refinement are interchangeable: they need not be\n   475\t(a guest set encoding a disjoint triangle and square as ordered pairs of\n   476\tequal-body cursor cells leaves all seven cursor cells in one class, and no\n   477\tautomorphism exchanges a triangle vertex with a square vertex). The\n   478\tprocedure therefore explores every unresolved alternative, with no\n   479\tpruning, and the representative it returns is canonical because the\n   480\tprocedure is deterministic and renaming-invariant, not because of any\n   540\t   contributing no step. The categories, and their one spelling each:\n   541\t   - *Fixed slot* (any tabled slot that is not one of the categories\n   542\t     below, including a `:pending` row's `cursor-cell-C` slots):\n   543\t     `[kind slot-index]`, the slot's 0-based index in the row table.\n   544\t   - *Ordered repeated entry* (`:vec`, `:list` elements; `:k`\n   545\t     frames; the root's `frames`): `[kind i]` with `i` the 0-based\n   546\t     position; for `frames` the step is `[:task :frame i]`.\n   547\t   - *Unordered element* (`:set`): `[kind :elem CE(e)]`; never an index.\n   548\t   - *Keyed pair* (`:map`, `:store`, `:bindings`, `:parked-table`, and\n   549\t     the root's installs and module-stores slots, keyed by module name\n   550\t     and `M`): `[kind :key CE(k)]` when descending into the key,\n   551\t     `[kind :val CE(k)]` when descending into the value; never an\n   552\t     index. For `:bindings`, `:parked-table`, installs and module\n   553\t     stores the key is a structural datum and `CE(k)` is the datum.\n   554\t   - *Task boundary*: a path never crosses into an install child; a\n   555\t     child's cursor cells have paths rooted at the child's own root.\n   556\t   Equal occurrences yield equal positions, one per occurrence, and\n   557\t   positions never contain a source enumeration index of an unordered\n   558\t   container.\n   559\t4. **Signature and refinement.** A cursor cell's signature is the CBOR of\n   560\t   `[:sig <old label> <sorted vector of its positions, duplicates\n   561\t   retained>]`; its new label is that byte string. Repeat until no\n   562\t   class splits. Keeping the old label makes refinement monotone, so\n   563\t   the partition stabilizes in at most `n − k` splitting rounds from\n   564\t   `k` initial classes plus one stability check; this bounds partition\n   565\t   rounds only, not signature-processing or search work.\n   566\t5. **Search.** Order classes bytewise by label. If every class is a\n   567\t   singleton, assign `1 … n` in that order and stop. Otherwise take the\n   568\t   first non-singleton class and, **for each of its members in turn**,\n   569\t   give that member the label that is the CBOR byte string of\n   570\t   `[:ind <depth> <old label>]`, where `depth` is 0 at the top-level\n   571\t   search and increases by one per level of recursion (distinct from\n   572\t   every refinement label by its tag; no ordering relative to other\n   573\t   labels is needed), refine to stability, and\n   574\t   recurse. Every branch is explored. Each complete leaf yields a\n   575\t   numbering; build the §5 rows under it and take the **root body's\n   576\t   canonical CBOR bytes** (the digest preimage, not the digest) as the\n   577\t   leaf's key. The procedure's output is the row set of the leaf with\n   578\t   the bytewise least key. Two leaves with equal keys have emitted\n   579\t   identical rows: they differ only in which source cursor cell received\n   580\t   which number, which the transported representation cannot observe.\n   581\t\n   582\t**Validation.** Canonicality is a property of the emitted rows, not of\n   583\ta source-cursor-cell-to-number bijection, so the receiver does not compare\n   584\tnumberings. It decodes the rows to the abstract task, runs the\n   585\tprocedure, re-emits rows, and compares the resulting root id with the\n   586\tcarried root id: unequal is `:yin.k/undecodable` kind\n   587\t`:noncanonical-cursor-cells`. Every labeling that yields the selected\n   588\tcommitment is thereby accepted, and no encounter-order tie-break ever\n   589\tdecides validity. This is a lower-side structural refusal, not a lift\n   590\tkind. A receiver whose work bound (§10.10) is exceeded before the\n   591\tprocedure completes refuses with a structured resource refusal before\n   592\tany attachment and never labels the state `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, never\n   593\tfalls back to encounter order, and never accepts an unfinished check.\n   594\t\n   595\tUnder this rule two lifts of one state are byte-identical. Two lifts of\n   596\tdifferent states sharing a closure over the same cursor cell may number it\n   597\tdifferently and so not share that closure's row across lifts; that\n   598\tcross-lift dedup is knowingly given up for identity-bearing values and\n   599\tnever affected rows below a cursor cell. On lower, each `C` becomes one fresh\n   600\tprivate resource entry seeded at its carried position; every `[:cursor-cell C]`\n   601\tmaps to that entry; two references to one cursor cell share it and one\n   602\treference per cursor cell keeps its own (UCF §7.5.3).\n   603\t\n   604\t## 7. Equality and the content address\n   605\t\n   606\tThe transported state is a DAG rooted at the `:task` row. Its address is\n   607\tthe root id, which commits to every reachable content row, to every cursor cell\n   608\tid through the references, and to every cursor cell's contents through the\n   609\tcensus. Two transported states are equal iff their root ids are equal,\n   610\tand under §6 that holds iff they were lifted from states equal up to the\n   611\trenaming of cursor-cell ids that §6 makes canonical. No physical enumeration of\n   612\tthe row set needs an order, because the root commits to everything and\n   613\tthe pack, if one is addressed, has its own canonical encoding (§10.2).\n   614\tJing supplies canonical bytes and the digest of each body; this document\n   615\tsupplies the order within each body and the numbering of cursor cells. Jing is\n   616\tasked to sort nothing it does not already sort.\n   617\t\n   618\tOccurrence and origin are inside the hash, as in versions 1 and 2 where\n   619\tthe body address is the hash of the whole body. Snapshot variants of one\n   620\toccurrence may therefore have distinct addresses while remaining one\n   621\toccurrence, exactly as UCF §7.3.4 intends.\n   622\t\n   623\t## 8. Validation on lower\n   624\t\n   625\tValidation is pure until the last step and checks the whole tree before\n   626\tone attachment. The order follows amendment §8 and is binding:\n   627\t\n   628\t1. **Gate.** Decode the wire map's canonical bytes retaining numeric\n   629\t   classes; the tag is present and the outer version is the exact\n   630\t   integer 3, else `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` (version found, supported\n   631\t   set). Reject duplicate row ids and a `:yin.k/root` that names no\n   632\t   `:task` row (`:yin.k/undecodable`). Walk install children from the\n   633\t   root in canonical module-name order with an **active recursion-path\n   634\t   set** (§3), following only `:install` child crefs; a cref outside the\n   635\t   rows, a child already on the active path, or a non-`:task` child\n   636\t   stops the gate as `:yin.k/undecodable`; a child reached again off\n   637\t   the path is gated once and its result cached. Gate every\n   638\t   child's version, then every profile map against the one profile map\n   639\t   of §2, then require all versions 3\n   640\t   and all profiles equal to the root's. Malformed task structure is\n   641\t   `:yin.k/undecodable`; an unsupported version or profile is\n   642\t   `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`; the two are never conflated.\n   643\t2. **Structure, non-recursive.** Every row's kind is tabled with the\n   644\t   right arity; every structural slot holds its tabled kind by local\n   645\t   inspection; every `V` has one of the three tags; every `D` is in the\n   646\t   canonical bytes domain; exactly one row has role `:root`; kind rules\n   647\t   of §5.5 hold; the custody slot matches the role, kind and policy\n   648\t   table. Nothing in this step follows a reference.\n   649\t3. **Graph.** Every cref and every `[:row B]` names a present row of a\n   650\t   kind admissible in that position; the structural edge family is\n   651\t   acyclic (checked with an active-path walk, bounded by the row count);\n   652\t   every row is reachable from the root through structural edges (an\n   653\t   unreachable row is `:yin.k/undecodable`); every `[:cursor-cell C]` names a\n   654\t   census entry and every census entry is reached **through the task's\n   655\t   own roots, the census's declaration edges excluded**, per task and\n   785\t   canonical encoding, distinct from the semantic root id; cursor-cell ids\n   786\t   remain root-scoped inside it. Same answer as code-as-tuples §2.1\n   787\t   should receive; the loader interface is resolved explicitly, not by\n   788\t   layout.\n   789\t3. **The nested grammar.** Rows are the carrier authority.\n   790\t4. **Contract stamp.** The code contract carried is `\"v4\"`, the\n   791\t   register-shaped machine's; the carrier version is 3; the two are\n   792\t   independent, and neither names a legacy value.\n   793\t5. **Reified and parked.** Sharing immutable `:act` rows is acceptable;\n   794\t   the two keep distinct outer kinds (§5.1) and distinct lowering. A\n   795\t   reified capture has no pending; a parked reference resolves in task\n   796\t   context.\n   797\t6. **Foreign-engine value profiles.** Required before an implementation\n   798\t   brief claims execution conformance for an engine **outside the three\n   799\t   repository lanes** (the semantic-register kernel and the stack and\n   800\t   register kernels, whose reconstruction is the layouts of\n   801\t   `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §4 and needs no value\n   802\t   profile), and not drafted here: admitted values, numeric behaviour,\n   803\t   key equality, metadata, resource and profile requirements, refusal\n   804\t   sets, and safepoint reconstruction obligations. Slot losslessness\n   805\t   alone does not establish execution parity; version 3 carries the\n   806\t   canonical frame; a stack or register kernel reconstructs it through\n   807\t   its layout (continuation §4), which is heterogeneous reconstruction,\n   808\t   not translation between native formats; foreign-engine *value*\n   809\t   profiles for engines outside this repository remain a separate\n   810\t   document.\n   811\t\n   812\tAnswers 7–9 are the Architect's (round 2) and are adopted (7 and 8 are\n   813\tdeleted 2026-10-11: there are no other profile tables and no legacy\n   814\treader):\n   815\t\n   816\t9. **Skeleton placeholder.** Safe only if the full value-union tag is\n   817\t   retained in the skeleton, which §6 now requires (`[:cursor-cell <class>]`,\n   818\t   never a bare class); and a placeholder does not canonicalize alias\n   819\t   topology, which is why §6 is now defined as the output of a\n   820\t   renaming-invariant refinement-and-search procedure.\n   821\t\n   822\t10. **Receiver work bound** (Architect, round 3; adopted as a\n   823\t    requirement, with the limits left to implementation and\n   824\t    composition). Before an implementation brief, the receiver must have\n   825\t    a bound on decoded bytes, rows, cursor cells, traversal depth, refinement\n   826\t    work and search nodes for §6, with elapsed time as an optional\n   827\t    operational limit on top. Exceeding a local budget produces a\n   828\t    structured resource or capability refusal before any attachment, in\n   829\t    the qualified-unsupported family `datom.world.md` already provides;\n   830\t    it never labels a valid state `:noncanonical-cursor-cells`, never falls\n   831\t    back to encounter order, and never accepts an unfinished check. The\n   832\t    exact limits and their refusal mapping are implementation and\n   833\t    composition decisions and must not alter canonical bytes.\n   834\t\n   835\t**Proposals, not consequences.** The following are design choices this\n   836\tdocument makes; they follow neither uniquely from the owner's three\n   837\trulings nor from the six invariants, and an implementation brief must\n   838\tname them as choices being accepted: a new body version (3) rather than\n   839\tanother carrier identification; the canonical representative of §6 as\n   840\tdefined by its procedure; the wire unit and pack framing of §3; the\n   841\texplicit fork-policy spelling of §5.5; one engine-less profile\n   842\t(continuation §2.1); the explicit root `free-env` (continuation §6.3);\n   843\tthe byte-string and metadata restrictions of §4; binding the row digest to\n   844\tthe carrier version rather than to a named algorithm (§3; the owner\n   845\truled 2026-10-10 that rows use the same digest as code addresses, which\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
