n   379\t    (or (ref? d) (= :C d)) (keyword? x)\n   380\t    (refs? d) (and (vector? x) (every? keyword? x))\n    14\t(branch `srvm-phase6a` at `d77da9f0`), and a read-only prototype run\n    15\tagainst that code (§6). Nothing here is implemented.\n    16\t\n    17\t**Recommendation in one line:** adopt discovery-order numbering now (§7,\n    18\toption a): a function of structure, renaming-invariant, linear work,\n    19\tprovable by hand; it deletes carrier §6's refinement and search and\n    20\tkeeps every pinned root id except the one state only the search could\n    21\tnumber.\n    22\t\n    23\t## 1. Findings\n    24\t\n    25\t**F1. Every non-guest position is ordered.** From the carrier §5 tables\n   330\t`[key value]` pairs; whichever of `'one` (`[:cursor-cell x]`), `'both`\n   331\t(`#{x y}`) or `'cursors` (`{x :x, y :y}`) sorts first, `x` is met before\n   332\t`y`, since `x` is alone under `'one` and its body (`:s1`) sorts before\n   333\t`y`'s (`:s2`) in the set and the map; so `x = cc-1`, `y = cc-2`. Review\n   334\tcounterexample: `'a` before `'b`; `#{X Y}` ties and is deferred; `'b`\n   335\tmeets `X = cc-1`; the fixpoint re-sorts the set, `[:n 1]` against a body\n   336\tlabel, and `Y = cc-2`. Alias `[x x y]`: `x = cc-1` at index 0, `y = cc-2`\n   337\tat index 2. The example state of `collab/example-suspended-state.clj`\n   338\thas one cursor cell, first met in the act's environment under `c`, so\n   339\t`cc-1`; a one-cell state has the same rows under both procedures.\n   340\t\n   341\t## 7. Recommendation\n   342\t\n   343\t**(a) Adopt discovery order now.** 6b has not started and 6a is\n   344\tunmerged, so the cost is one implementation slice of `rows.cljc` and its\n   345\ttests plus the amendments of §4: delete `check-label-bytes!`\n   346\t(`rows.cljc:212-230`), `positions` (`:285-325`), `classes` (`:326-330`),\n   347\t`refine` (`:331-337`), `search` (`:338-354`) and the label seeding\n   348\t(`:252-255`); keep `ce` (`:257-284`) with the numbered/unnumbered\n   349\tspelling; add the traversal, fixpoint, orbit rule and refusal (the\n   350\tprototype is 110 lines with helpers; 60-80 in place); delete the\n   351\t`:search` and `:label-bytes` budget keys (`:200-202`). Unchanged:\n   352\t`emit`, `emit-numbered`, `canonical-under`, the census and its numeric\n   353\torder (`:140-156`), `decode*`'s recompute-and-compare (`:570-575`),\n   354\tnumbering before `validate-frames` (`:576-578`; test\n   355\t`numbering-precedes-frame-defect`, `rows_test.cljc:206`), the `:bytes`,\n   356\t`:rows`, `:depth` and `:work` bounds. Tests: `rows_test.cljc:171`\n   357\tbecomes the orbit-rule test (no `{:search 1}`); `:307-329` keeps\n   358\t`fab223…` and `c4a7c7…`, drops `55ff168e…`, `{:search 2}` and `cc-3`;\n   359\t`:400-404` becomes the D5 refusal test; `:406-421` is deleted. Cost:\n   360\tone implementation round and one review round, and the review can check\n   361\t§3 by hand. Risk: a canonicality bug, mitigated by §8 item 18's\n   362\tgenerator in CI and by the proof; and the D5 class, documented and\n   363\tnarrowable later without id churn.\n   364\t\n   365\t**(b) Keep the 6a design.** Zero rounds now, but 6b, the cross-engine\n   366\tharness and every reviewer of a pinned id inherit an exhaustive search,\n   367\tlabels that grow until the seven-cell state exceeds a megabyte, and a\n   368\tdefinition that is \"whatever the procedure outputs\". Not recommended.\n   369\t\n   370\t**(c) Portable ids.** Changes the VM, the census, the laws and the\n   371\tharness (§5); three or more rounds across two designs. Against.\n   372\t\n   373\t## 8. Acceptance for the rewritten 6a numbering\n   374\t\n   375\t12. `rows-test/discovery-order-numbering`: for `fixture :s1 :s2 :x :y`,\n20:(§3), the static laws use actual-successor live-out (§5.6), blinding is\n225:`:yin.k/cc-<n>` numbered by the draft's §6 procedure; the root carries\n755:value per name). The round-trip law is therefore stated on **canonical\n1170:   wrappers, §5.2), on the reference lane; laws 1-3 and 6; counts\n1256:10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n1258:11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n1318:  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n1555:In §9's law list delete \"Exact mutual inversion is required only between\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-HpfDxzRx' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-12 02:41:05.313 xcodebuild[75721:57373826]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-12 02:41:05.661 xcodebuild[75721:57373824] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-ODzGq3yQ' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-12 02:41:06.429 xcodebuild[75725:57373849]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-12 02:41:06.707 xcodebuild[75725:57373848] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n  2308\t    (fail \"Cannot resume: parked continuation not found\"\n  2309\t          {:parked-id parked-id})))\n  2310\t\n  2311\t\n  2312\t(defn gensym\n  2313\t  \"Generate a unique ID and return [id updated-state].\"\n  2314\t  ([state] (gensym state \"id\"))\n  2315\t  ([state prefix]\n  2316\t   (let [id-counter (or (:id-counter state) 0)\n  2317\t         id (gen-id prefix id-counter)]\n  2318\t     [id (assoc state :id-counter (inc id-counter))])))\n  2319\t\n  2320\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"comple