ts of `:pending` rows, and the keys of the `:cursor-cells` census.\n   501\t   - `[:lit d]` → `[:lit d]`.\n   502\t   - `[:cursor-cell C]`, and a bare `C` slot → `[:cursor-cell <label of C>]` (full\n   503\t     tag retained, §10.9).\n   504\t   - `[:row B]` → `[:row <CE(row B)>]`, the row expanded in place; the\n   505\t     expansion is finite because the structural edge family is acyclic\n   506\t     (§8 step 3).\n   507\t   - A row `[kind s₁ … sₖ]` → `[kind CE(s₁) … CE(sₖ)]` with each slot\n   508\t     encoded as: a structural datum (`A`, `M`, `P`, `S`, `N`, `D`, a\n   509\t     reason, a phase, a version, a role, a kind) as itself; a `C` as\n   510\t     above; a `V` as above; a cref as the expanded row; a crefs vector\n   511\t     as the vector of expansions.\n   512\t   - For `:set` rows, and for the key-value pairs of `:map`, `:store`\n   513\t     and `:bindings` rows, the entries of `:parked-table`, and the\n   514\t     installs and module-stores slots of the root: encode each element\n   515\t     (or each `[key value]` pair as a two-element vector), then **sort\n   516\t     the resulting vector of encodings bytewise, retaining duplicates**.\n   517\t     Ordered rows (`:vec`, `:list`, `:k`) and the ordered\n   518\t     `frames` slot keep their order.\n   519\t   - The `:cursor-cells` census is **not expanded**: in `CE(root)` the\n   520\t     `cursor-cells-cref` slot is the constant `[:cursor-cells]`. The census is a\n   521\t     derived index of the cursor cells the task reaches, so it carries no\n   522\t     additional information beyond the reached cursor cell identities and\n   523\t     their bodies (which already seed the initial labels), and\n   524\t     (consistently with\n   525\t     §8 step 3, which excludes census declaration edges from\n   526\t     reachability) **census declaration occurrences contribute no\n   527\t     positions** to any cursor cell.\n   528\t   - Context lookups (`P` in `:parked-ref` and `parked-id`, `M` in\n  