{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'Terminology: cursor|minted by the emitter|non-portable|unresolved' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | head -20; sed -n '77,103p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md; git diff --stat; nl -ba collab/numbering-probe/src/probe/discovery.clj | sed -n '194,214p'\"","aggregated_output":"268:Lift adds these kinds to the `:yin.k/non-portable` set of 7.5.4:\n467:  `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind :non-canonicalizable`).\n1017:  else lift refuses `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:install-response`.\n1056:  `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:incomplete-install`, before\n1102:  an enrolled stream refuses the lift as `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind\n1152:| anything else | — | — | **refused**: `:yin.k/non-portable` |\n1221:lower-side refusal (`yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3), not a `:yin.k/non-portable`\n1256:the lift immediately, as `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind\n1298:  (`:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:ambiguous-primitive`) unless the\n1344:  as `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind :cyclic` naming the path. The\n1358:**Terminology: cursor, cursor cell, cursor-ref, cell.** The specification\n1400:Cursor-cell ids are minted by the emitter (stable within one lift; remapped on\n1430:non-portable or unsatisfied outcomes; a missing remote attachment is\n1439:{:yin.k/status :yin.k/non-portable\n1629:refuses the lift, as `:yin.k/non-portable` with `:yin.k/kind\n1670:  refuses the lift (`:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:foreign-parked-ref`),\n1918:`:link-request` entry without `:cursor` -- as `:yin.k/non-portable`,\n2006:header refuses `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:op-seq-exhausted`, at the\n2240:   of that task refuses `:yin.k/non-portable`, kind\n2661:| `:yin.k/non-portable` | lift | `:yin.k/path`, `:yin.k/kind`, `:yin.k/hint` — kinds at §7.5.4, cycles included as `:kind :cyclic` |\nPhase 5 is three pure functions of an admitted register-shaped vector\n`v` (A = `ucf/code-address v`). `resolve` (§1) rewrites every `:var` to\n`:load-bound`/`:load-free` and every `:closure` to its arity, using the\nclosure-owner tree the validator already established; its output is the\n*resolved vector*, same pcs, same virtual registers, a stage value with\nno identity. `register-image` (§2) allocates physical temporaries per\nbody by a linear scan over intervals computed from the phase-3 liveness\n`L`, fills the `live` operands with the format's one liveness function,\nand emits the existing `:yin.debruijn.register/*` image; the allocation\nrule is the frozen §8.2's, closed where that text left choices open and\ncorrected in one place (§9.1 F8). `stack-image` (§3) emits the existing\n`:yin.debruijn.code/*` image by one walk over the parse trees the\nvalidator recovers: operator, push, operands with pushes, call, labels\nfor conditionals, bodies out of line in FIFO order. Neither function\nreads the tree, a side table, or anything but `v`; neither calls an old\nlowerer. The image formats, descriptors, validators and kernels are\nunchanged, so every existing refusal rule, the `live-exact` recomputation\nand the kernels' execution semantics still admit and run the new images.\nThe hand-derived goldens of §6.3 fix the bytes for `(+ 1 2)`,\n`(f (g x) y)`, `((f))`, two conditionals, a tail call, two definitions and\na terminal operand; the execution oracle of §6.1 runs every corpus\nprogram through the old and new pipelines on the same kernels and\nrequires identical observable results; §4 shows, with evidence, that\nthe facts A omits cannot reach R or H. The scanners (§7) are unchanged\nfrom the reviewed design.\n\n---\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-nSlCSGy1' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-12 02:42:01.366 xcodebuild[75929:57375048]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-12 02:42:01.561 xcodebuild[75929:57375047] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-SuLXVaWm' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-12 02:42:02.115 xcodebuild[75932:57375067]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-12 02:42:02.311 xcodebuild[75932:57375066] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n   194\t    (go n)))\n   195\t\n   196\t(defn gen-value\n   197\t  \"Random V over cells; depth-bounded. Returns V.\"\n   198\t  [^java.util.Random r cells depth]\n   199\t  (let [pick (fn [xs] (nth xs (.nextInt r (count xs))))\n   200\t        k (.nextInt r (if (pos? depth) 6 3))]\n   201\t    (case k\n   202\t      0 [:lit (pick [1 2 :k \"s\" nil])]\n   203\t      1 [:cursor-cell (pick cells)]\n   204\t      2 [:cursor-cell (pick cells)]\n   205\t      3 [:row (rows/node :vec (vec (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth)))))]\n   206\t      4 (let [elems (vec (distinct (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 4)) #(gen-value r cells (dec depth)))))]\n   207\t          (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) elems) [:row (rows/node :set elems)] [:lit (set (map second elems))]))\n   208\t      5 (let [pairs (vec (vals (into {} (map (fn [p] [(pr-str (first p)) p]))\n   209\t                                     (repeatedly (inc (.nextInt r 3)) #(vector (gen-value r cells (dec depth)) (gen-value r cells (dec depth)))))))]\n   210\t          (if (some (fn [[a b]] (or (not= :lit (first a)) (not= :lit (first b)))) pairs)\n   211\t            [:row (rows/node :map (vec (mapcat identity pairs)))]\n   212\t            [:lit (into {} (map (fn [[a b]] [(second a) (second b)])) pairs)])))))\n   213\t\n   214\t(defn reached [v]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
